<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-12369] JdbcThinClient and Server compatibility broken</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-12369</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Query cancellation support was introduced in &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-5439&quot; title=&quot;JDBC thin: support query cancel&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-5439&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-5439&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. From this time server expects that ALL request have id. It breaks compatibility with clients whose version prior to 2.8.0.&lt;br/&gt;
Furthermore backport of this feature to 8.7 breaks compatibility newer build of server with older build of client.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;See &lt;tt&gt;ClientListenerProcessor#makeFilters&lt;/tt&gt;. New filter with overrided&#160;&lt;em&gt;onMessageReceived&lt;/em&gt;&#160;is created here. It tries to read request id and if there is not enough data to read long value, it crashes.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
